[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2942584057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-2942584057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":2942584057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vZET5","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T02:56:28Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T02:56:28Z","body":"After doing a quick and very unscientific benchmark, it seems like using `TypedArray<FuzzyMatch>` instead of `Vector<FuzzySearchResult>` is about 5-10% slower for the quick open dialog use case, or .1-.2ms for a project of mine with a few hundred resources. I think the original PR saw a more significant speed difference because refcounted instances were used internally to the algorithm at that point and not just for the returned values, so several times more refcounted instances would be created per search.\r\n\r\nWith that in mind, to me it doesn't seem worth having both sets of methods around but I do think working with the `Vector<FuzzySearchResult>` is marginally nicer since there are no variant conversions. The non-refcounted type would still need to exist for internal use. I could go either way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2942584057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4276769479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4276769479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4276769479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-6lLH","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-19T20:38:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T20:41:43Z","body":"Not sure if there is continued interest in adding this for script access but I rebased and retested the changes. It seems like a convenient thing to expose but maybe it would encourage further noise and tweaks for the algo/scoring.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4276769479/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4375466762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4375466762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4375466762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBMxTCg","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T23:59:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T23:59:28Z","body":"Thank you for the thorough review! Looking at the full pr with fresh eyes I wish I caught some of these convention/scope issues myself haha. I've updated the branch; I'll push it up after re-testing and running a sketchy benchmark.\r\n\r\nI am a bit confused by:\r\n\r\n> Following that example it would suggest only having the `RefCounted` API is the way to go. I would lean towards that as well.\r\n\r\n> [...]\r\n\r\n> The way you're doing it now, with having a special bound method that returns `TypedArray`, is how I'm used to seeing it. You obviously need `TypedArray` for the script bindings and it should ideally not be forced upon the internal C++ usage, in my opinion.\r\n> \r\n> Funnily enough this sort of goes against using `RegEx` as reference, since it does in fact use `TypedArray<RegExMatch>` in its `search_all`, but I would probably argue that should not be the case.\r\n\r\nAre you saying that only having the RefCounted api would match existing convention more closely, and so it could be worth doing for that reason, but the slightly better performance/ergonomics of the non-variant api for engine use outweighs that?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4375466762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4376188806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4376188806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4376188806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBNdXhg","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T02:44:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T02:44:47Z","body":"I ended up using `FuzzySearchMatch` for the refcounted type and `FuzzySearchMatchData` for the internal type but super easy to change those names again. I can make the change to combine the two of them but with score filtering there's generally an order of magnitude more values pre filtering than post on my test project so I don't really want to introduce 100s of totally unused refcounted instances per call. Adding the reserve for the token match vector is marginally faster (~.12ms, 3.5% for me) but it's pretty high variance.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4376188806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4378487031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4378487031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4378487031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBPpo9w","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T10:39:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T10:39:21Z","body":"> Are you saying that only having the RefCounted api would match existing convention more closely, and so it could be worth doing for that reason, but the slightly better performance/ergonomics of the non-variant api for engine use outweighs that?\r\n\r\nI meant that since `RegEx` is a similar-looking API, its use of `RefCounted` for `RegExMatch` would justify using that here as well, but when it comes to whether or not `search_all` should use `TypedArray<...>` or `Vector<Ref<...>>` we might want to ignore that part and just go with two methods instead, one private script-bound method that returns `TypedArray<FuzzySearchMatch>` and one public that returns `Vector<Ref<FuzzySearchMatch>>`, i.e. still using `RefCounted` everywhere.\r\n\r\nMy motivation for saying that was mostly ergonomics and type-safety (and maybe a tiny bit performance) since the type argument to `TypedArray` has no compile-time effect at all, meaning there's nothing stopping you from assigning the results to a `TypedVector<GLTFMesh>` or whatever.\r\n\r\nI don't know how much of a practical problem that really is though. There's certainly plenty of C++ use of `TypedArray` in the engine already, so I could be wrong about this.\r\n\r\n> I can make the change to combine the two of them but with score filtering there's generally an order of magnitude more values pre filtering than post on my test project so I don't really want to introduce 100s of totally unused refcounted instances per call.\r\n\r\nI do think it looks a bit odd to have them both, but I don't feel strongly enough one way or the other to push back on this again, so I'd say let's leave this as-is for now and we'll see if the next reviewer feels differently.\r\n\r\n> Adding the reserve for the token match vector is marginally faster (~.12ms, 3.5% for me) but it's pretty high variance.\r\n\r\nYeah, page faults (i.e. when the OS actually goes to allocate physical memory) is what makes heap allocations costly usually, and can happen \"randomly\" depending on other allocations in the application.\r\n\r\n(Making everything `RefCounted` would of course also make them individually heap-allocated, which is not ideal for the same reason. `reserve` was mostly just a simple one-liner win at no cost to readability/maintainability.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4378487031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4383549192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4383549192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4383549192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBUenCA","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T22:14:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T22:14:15Z","body":"Did another rough benchmark and although having only the refcounted result type is ~20% slower, that's only ~.8ms on my laptop (m2 macbook air) so maybe that's an appropriate performance cost for this feature. I also checked the quick open search and it seemed like although it was overall slower, it wasn't additionally slower on top of the fuzzy search timing change. For now, I'll push up the changes as two commits and if that's the desired route I'll squash them later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4383549192/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391089220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4391089220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4391089220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbq0RA","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T19:07:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T19:08:22Z","body":"Squashed + applied lint fixes. Last question of mine is if I should mark the new api experimental or does it feel stable enough as it is? Also, would it make sense to expose a static search/search_all which uses the default configuration?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391089220/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4480370325","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107126#issuecomment-4480370325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107126","id":4480370325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCw0GlQ","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-jo